      "writtenOn": "2025-02-26T16:57:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The x86 task_id field will be 0. x86 is the only arch that has this field, so there isn\u0027t really a way to set it with these macros. For software panics, the task id is placed in the info field. This will certinley cause some confusion down the road when debugging a software panic. The task id will be 0, and the actual task id will be in the error_code field (using host/panic.c mapping). \n\nFixing this is beyond the scope of this CL. It will require a revision of the panic data struct.",
      "revId": "ec3902a927db85fb7eea81295f2c293df596b1e1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
